Inheritance in Java is a mechanism in which one object acquires all the properties and behaviors of a parent object.
Inheritance represents the IS-A relationship which is also known as a parent-child relationship. 
Using Extends keyword we can achieve inheritance.
Advantages: reusability, method overiding, loose coupling, Supports polymorphism.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. extends Keyword Rules:
    A class can extend only one class
    A class can implement multiple interfaces
    extends also used by interface to extend another interface

2. Constructor Inheritance:
    Constructors are not inherited
    Parent constructor executes first

3. final with Inheritance:
    final class	Cannot be inherited
    final method	Cannot be overridden
    final variable	Cannot be changed

4. Inheritance vs Composition (Very Important)
    | Inheritance             | Composition        |
    | ----------------------- | ------------------ |
    | IS-A                    | HAS-A              |
    | Tight coupling          | Loose coupling     |
    | Less flexible           | More flexible      |
    | Compile-time dependency | Runtime dependency |

5. Memory & JVM Perspective:
    Parent & child methods loaded in Method Area
    Object created only for child
    Parent variables are part of child object
    Constructor chaining happens top-down

