Advanced Features (Java 8+):-
Static Methods: Belong to the interface itself, not to instances.
Functional Interfaces: Interfaces with a single abstract method (SAM), used in lambda expressions. Example: Runnable, Comparator.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Types: single, multilevel, hierarichal, multiple level inheritance.
1. Single inheritance: when one class inherits properties and behaviours of parent class.

2. multi level: class A->class B->class C
     
3. Hierarchical Inheritance: Class A, Class B, Class C ----> Class D 
When two or more classes inherits a single class, it is known as hierarchical inheritance.

4. Multiple Inheritance: 
    class A { void show() {} }
  class B { void show() {} }
  // class C extends A, B ❌

     this can result in issues like the diamond problem, 
    which occurs when two superclasses share the same method or field and causes conflicts.
    Java uses interfaces to implement multiple inheritances in order to prevent these conflicts.

5. Hybrid Inheritance:
    The hybrid inheritance is the composition of two or more types of inheritance. The main purpose of using hybrid inheritance is to modularize the code into well-defined classes.
   Classes Son, Daughter -----> class Father-----> class GrandPa

14. Inheritance in Spring Boot

    ❌ Not recommended for business logic
    ✅ Prefer interfaces + composition
    Service Layer Example
    @Service
    class BaseService {
        void log() {
            System.out.println("Logging");
        }
    }
    
    @Service
    class UserService extends BaseService {
        void process() {
            log();
        }
    }

