FAQs about Inheritance:
1. Why multiple inheritance is not supported in Java?
    To reduce the complexity and simplify the language, multiple inheritance is not supported in Java.

Common Tricky Interview Questions (4+ Years):

Q1. Can we override static method?
❌ No — it is method hiding.

Q2. Can we reduce visibility while overriding?
❌ No — can only increase.

Q3. Why Java doesn’t support multiple inheritance?
    To avoid ambiguity & complexity.

Q4. Is inheritance mandatory for polymorphism?
❌ No (interfaces also support it).

Q5. Can private methods be overridden?
❌ No — they are not inherited.

Q6. Can constructor be overridden?
❌ No — constructors are not inherited.

